# Hints for agents working on this repository

## Language

- The conversation with the owner is **always in Italian**.
- Code, comments, string literals, identifiers, file names, commit messages
  and all documentation (README, these hints) are **always in English**.
- When the owner writes in Italian, answer in Italian; never translate the
  code or the docs back into Italian.

## Project

`android-eye` is the behaviour test bench for a wall-mounted android face on a
staircase: a PIR and an ultrasonic sensor decide when the eyelid opens.

- `android_eye_test/android_eye_test.ino` is the whole firmware.
- `README.md` documents hardware, wiring, states and tuning.
- There is no test suite: the bench is the Arduino itself.

## Rules

- The sketch must keep compiling for both `CON_PIR 0` and `CON_PIR 1`.
- Every tunable value lives in the constant block at the top of the sketch.
  Add new ones there; never scatter magic numbers through the logic.
- Opening/closing asymmetry (`T_OPEN` 620 ms vs `T_CLOSE` 2600 ms) is a design
  decision, not a bug. Do not equalise them.
- Arduino requires the folder name to match the sketch name: never rename
  `android_eye_test/`.
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*. Keep them short and in English.
- Do not commit, push or tag unless the owner asks.
